# KSV-0024 — k8s/webui/deployment.yaml sets a Pod hostPort (3000). Deliberate, not an oversight:
# keeps the k3s deployment's :3000 reachable at the same address/bookmarks as the Docker
# deployment it's meant to replace, on a single-node cluster. Revisit (Ingress/LoadBalancer
# instead) before any multi-node move — see k8s/webui/deployment.yaml's own comment on that port.
# Rule-ID ignore here, not an inline `# trivy:ignore:` comment: verified (pinned
# aquasec/trivy:0.74.0, tested locally) that this specific rule doesn't honor an inline comment
# for Kubernetes manifests in this version, at any position tried.
KSV-0024 exp:2027-01-01
